Phase 5 Task 2 — HUD police-button pulse hint (FR6)

Implementation:
- VehicleHud gains setPolicePulse(pulsing): toggles `is-pulsing` on the
  police button (buttons-map lookup).
- index.html: `police-pulse` keyframes — brightness(1 <-> 1.22) +
  scale(1 <-> 1.09) at 1.1s ease-in-out infinite, on
  .hud-button--police.is-pulsing only. The standalone `scale` property is
  animated rather than `transform` so the active button's lift (is-active
  transform) survives the pulse; the small police button can never visually
  compete with the 96px ability button.
- main.ts: startPuppy() sets the pulse right after the whine
  (puppyPending = true); onSirenCast() clears it the moment the siren
  answers (puppyPending = false). puppyPending has no other writers or
  clearers, so pulse and pending flag cannot drift apart.

Gates: pnpm check clean; pnpm typecheck clean; CI=true pnpm test 516/516
(43 files, unchanged — HUD glue is manual-verify per plan).

Manual verification steps (dev server http://localhost:5173/):
1. Let the rotation reach the lost-puppy round: whine sounds and the police
   HUD button breathes (gentle scale + brighten, 1.1s loop).
2. It reads as an invitation and does NOT outshine the ability button
